.TH FOSSH\-CONSOLE 1 "2026-08-15" "foSSH 0.2.0" "foSSH Manual"
.SH NAME
fossh\-console \- desktop console for administering a foSSH install
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fossh\-console
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fossh\-console
is the local administration interface for a foSSH install. It shows
what each site recorded today, runs k\-anonymised queries against the
rollup store, manages external services added with an API key, and
drives first\-run operator enrollment.
.PP
It takes no arguments and opens nothing it was not started with. All
of its data comes from
.BR fossh\-agent (8),
a helper process it spawns over a pipe; the console itself never
listens on a socket and holds no credential longer than the call that
carries it.
.SH "PRIVACY BEHAVIOUR WORTH KNOWING"
Breakdowns are folded before they reach this window. Any group with
fewer than
.I k_anonymity
estimated unique visitors (default 5) is combined into a single
.B (other)
row inside the store's own query engine, so no read path can bypass
it. On a low\-traffic site this is the normal case, not a malfunction,
and the Telemetry page says so explicitly rather than drawing an empty
chart.
.PP
Totals are unaffected by the fold; only per\-group breakdowns can
disappear this way.
.SH "API KEYS"
A key added under Integrations is sealed on disk under the install's
own data key and is never sent back to this window. The list shows at
most the last four characters, and only when the key is long enough
for four to be a hint rather than most of it. There is no way to
reveal a stored key from the interface, because the interface does not
have it. Replacing a key means removing the integration and adding it
again.
.PP
Plain
.B http://
is refused for anything but a loopback address: a key sent over it is
readable by anything on the path.
.SH "KEYBOARD"
.TP
.BR Ctrl+R ", " F5
Refresh the current page.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+1 " .. " Ctrl+4
Jump to Overview, Telemetry, Integrations or Setup.
.TP
.B Ctrl+?
Show the keyboard shortcuts.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FOSSH_DATA_DIR
The install's data directory. Default
.IR /var/lib/fossh .
.TP
.B FOSSH_AGENT_BIN
Path to the helper binary, for running against a build tree. Default
.IR /usr/libexec/fossh/fossh\-agent .
.TP
.B FOSSH_K_ANONYMITY
Overrides the k\-anonymity threshold the helper reports. An explicit
.B 0
is rejected and the safe default used instead, because a threshold of
zero does not weaken the guarantee, it removes it.
.TP
.B FOSSH_SETUP_TOKEN_PATH
Where the watchdog's one\-time setup token is read from. Default
.IR /etc/fossh/setup\-token .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/fossh/fossh.db
The rollup store this console reads.
.TP
.I /var/lib/fossh/integrations.enc
Configured external services, sealed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on a clean quit. A failure to start the helper is reported
in the window rather than on exit, so that an operator who launched
this from a desktop menu sees it.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR fossh (1),
.BR fossh\-fcgi (8),
.BR fossh\-watchdog (8)
.PP
.IR /usr/share/doc/fossh/README.md ,
.I /usr/share/doc/fossh-console/RETIREMENT.md
.SH NOTES
This console replaces the
.B fossh\-tui
terminal interface shipped up to 0.1.3. That release line is retired;
see RETIREMENT.md for what was wrong with it.
.PP
.B fossh\-agent
always runs as whoever launches this console, never as a service (see
DESCRIPTION). On a fresh install this package's own
.I %post
joins its files to the
.B fossh\-console
group already, but on an upgrade of a session already logged in, or of
the base package alone without this one, the running user may need
.RS
.EX
usermod \-a \-G fossh\-console $USER
.EE
.RE
followed by logging out and back in, before
.I /var/lib/fossh
is reachable and this console shows real data instead of "This install
has no data directory yet."
